1
00:00:54,285 --> 00:01:00,285
Man Searching for Immortality/Woman Searching for Eternity
is a drama film directed by Bill Viola.

2
00:01:48,571 --> 00:01:54,571
Two naked, life-sized figures, each around 70 years old, track torches across
their aging epidermises as if rooting out the pattern of their pasts.

3
00:02:42,857 --> 00:02:48,857
The skin itself becomes a metaphor for lived experience
and the prospect of its termination.

4
00:03:37,142 --> 00:03:43,142
Performer, played by Luis Accinelli.

5
00:04:31,428 --> 00:04:37,428
Performer, played by Penny Safranek.

6
00:05:25,714 --> 00:05:31,714
Wings of Desire (German: Der Himmel über Berlin,
pronounced [deːɐ̯ ˈhɪml̩ ˈʔyːbɐ bɛɐ̯ˈliːn] ; lit.

7
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:26,000
'The Heaven/Sky over Berlin') is a 1987 romantic fantasy film written by Wim
Wenders, Peter Handke and Richard Reitinger, and directed by Wenders.

8
00:07:14,285 --> 00:07:20,285
The film is about invisible, immortal angels who populate Berlin and listen to
the thoughts of its human inhabitants, comforting the distressed.

9
00:08:08,571 --> 00:08:14,571
Even though the city is densely populated, many of the people
are isolated or estranged from their loved ones.

10
00:09:02,857 --> 00:09:08,857
One of the angels, played by Bruno Ganz, falls in love with a
beautiful, lonely trapeze artist, played by Solveig Dommartin.

11
00:09:57,142 --> 00:10:03,142
The angel chooses to become mortal so that he can experience human sensory pleasures, ranging from enjoying
food to touching a loved one, and so that he can discover human love with the trapeze artist.

12
00:10:51,428 --> 00:10:57,428
Inspired by art depicting angels visible around West Berlin, at the time encircled by the Berlin Wall, Wenders and author Peter
Handke conceived of the story and continued to develop the screenplay throughout the French and German co-production.

13
00:11:45,714 --> 00:11:51,714
The film was shot by Henri Alekan in both colour and black-and-white, the
latter being used to represent the world as seen by the angels.

14
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:46,000
The cast includes Otto Sander, Curt Bois and Peter Falk.

15
00:13:34,285 --> 00:13:40,285
For Wings of Desire, Wenders won awards for Best Director at both
the Cannes Film Festival and European Film Awards.

16
00:14:28,571 --> 00:14:34,571
The film was a critical and financial success, and academics have interpreted it as a statement of the importance of
cinema, libraries, the circus, or German unity, containing New Age, religious, secular or other themes.

17
00:15:22,857 --> 00:15:28,857
It was followed by a sequel, Faraway, So Close!, released in 1993.

18
00:16:17,142 --> 00:16:23,142
City of Angels, a U.S.

19
00:17:11,428 --> 00:17:17,428
remake, was released in 1998.

20
00:18:05,714 --> 00:18:11,714
In 1990, numerous critics named Wings of Desire as
one of the best films of the 1980s.
